===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|miluh|lang=goh}}, akin to {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|miluk|lang=osx}}. Compare {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|mælk|lang=da}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|melk|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|molke|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|melk|lang=no}}, {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|meolc|lang=ang}}, English {{term|milk}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|mjölk|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|yi|-}} {{term|מילך|sc=Hebr|tr=milkh|lang=yi}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|g=f|plural=Milchen|pl2=Milche}}


# [[milk|Milk]]
# [[white|White]] [[fluid]] that is [[exuded]] by certain [[plants]]
# A [[white]] [[liquid]] that is a [[mixture]] of other [[substances]], where one of the components is very finely distributed
# [[semen|Semen]] of male [[fish]]

